{
  "_meta": {
    "title": "v8p9 infer-sweep candidate (focus: keep SR≈1.0 while reducing path length/time)",
    "date": "2026-02-24",
    "summary": "v8p9 is an inference-first iteration: tune admissibility gating and replacement scoring to reduce avg_path_length/path_time_s under shielded/hybrid regime, without changing goal tolerances (anti-cheat). Training section is kept aligned with v8p8 (dueling + globalcnn_fusion + aux admissibility) for potential follow-up training.",
    "commands": [
      "conda run -n ros2py310 python train.py --profile v8p9",
      "conda run -n ros2py310 python infer.py --profile v8p9"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "Anti-cheating: do NOT change goal_tolerance_m (and do not loosen stop thresholds) for evaluation.",
      "Final gate C must use fixed pairs20 for short/long with runs=20 each."
    ]
  },
